    "text": "Begin the servos with a soft whine.\n\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\nBegin the servos with a soft whine. Unit 734’s optical sensors flickered, adjusting to the relentless downpour that turned the neon-drenched streets into a kaleidoscope of blurred lights. The package, heavy and sealed with crimson wax, felt unnervingly warm against its chassis. Rain slicked its metallic plating, threatening to short-circuit its delicate circuits, but the delivery window was absolute.\n\nAs it navigated the crowded market, a sudden gust of wind snatched a child’s red balloon from a weeping girl’s grip. Before the unit could process the loss, its manipulator arm extended, catching the string just inches from the muddy gutter. It gently handed the tattered toy back, the girl’s tear-streaked face breaking into a fragile smile. The warmth in the package seemed to pulse in approval.\n\nUnit 734 continued its path, the weight of the cargo feeling less like a burden and more like a promise kept.\n\nTrue efficiency is measured not by speed, but by the humanity we preserve in the machine."
